I go to the checkout.
I put the groceries onto the conveyor belt.
My shopping basket is empty now.
The cashier scans my groceries.
He scans the tomatoes, the apples, the cheese and the kohlrabi.
He also scans the rice, the pasta and the coffee.
He looks at me.
"That is twenty-five Euro, please," he says.
I open my wallet.
I do not have exactly twenty-five Euro.
I take a fifty-Euro note.
The cashier takes the banknote.
I take the change.
"Would you like the receipt?" he asks.
"No, thank you," I answer.
I do not need a receipt.
I pack my groceries into the cloth bags.
Now I want to go home.
